statement:
Let $n \in \bbn$, and identify the set of $n$-bit Boolean inputs with $\{0,1\}^n$. For $x, y \in \{0,1\}^n$, write $\langle x, y\rangle = \bigoplus_{i=1}^{n} (x_i \wedge y_i) \in \{0,1\}$ for their mod-$2$ inner product, so that $(-1)^{\langle x, y\rangle}$ equals $+1$ when $\langle x, y\rangle = 0$ and $-1$ when $\langle x, y\rangle = 1$. Then for every subset $B \subseteq \{0,1\}^n$,
\[
  \sum_{x \in \{0,1\}^n}
    \Bigl(\, \sum_{y \in B} (-1)^{\langle x, y\rangle} \Bigr)^{2}
  \;\le\; \bigl(2^{n}\bigr)^{2}.
\]
